/target
/dist
/.kaeru-vault/
*.swp
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
.intentionally-empty-file.*

# The vendored tree is verified byte-for-byte against the SHA-256 digests in
# each crate's `.cargo-checksum.json`, so nothing inside it may be ignored.
# Without this, the unanchored patterns above (`.vscode/`, `.idea/`, `*.swp`,
# `.DS_Store`) silently drop files that upstream crates ship — e.g.
# `vendor/cxx-1.0.194/.vscode/` — and every build then fails with
# "failed to open file ... No such file or directory".
!vendor/**
